      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The struggle itself is a profound act of self-preservation, even if the outcome feels fixed. If you truly believe the end is unavoidable, then the only thing left to control is the quality of the journey until then. Instead of fighting the tide, perhaps you could find a way to simply ride it, letting the effort of *trying* become a small, manageable act of defiance against the darkness.",
      "source": "target",
